  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Floating-point errors still plague the quick menu.  The main quick menu panel has been improved to account for motion to a certain degree, but the wing drag sensitivity is so small that it's essentially impossible to switch avatars while in the air for example because it just slides the menu a tiny bit instead of selecting.  When far enough out or moving fast enough, the entire menu becomes unusable and makes that 'boop' sound of highlighting stuff rapidly as the laser is highlighting random things every frame.  This has happened to me often enough that sometimes the spamming of the 'boop' sound echoes in my head.\n\nSometimes it is so bad that it is nigh impossible to respawn in order to use the menu again.  Usually i futilely attempt to click really fast until i luck out and it hits the respawn.",
